PATCH 531: the four 5acc/5b41/5bb6/5c2b paint siblings, and 584a's [0x61a] call (board:0014).

Patch 190 already worked this out ONCE, for FUN_0000_584a, and said so at the site:

    "the nested paint method [0x6c8]=294d (587f `call [0x6c8]`) is reached with ax=the popped UNMASKED
     value (sprite-directory offset = 294d param_1) and bx=node+4 (position descriptor = 294d param_4).
     Patch 181 dropped BOTH -> 294d/298a blitted a garbage sprite (runaway 298a SIGSEGV)."

Its four siblings -- FUN_0000_5acc, 5b41, 5bb6, 5c2b (patches 182/183) -- have the identical body and
were left calling `(ax)` alone.  All four asm bodies are the same instruction for instruction, differing
only in the sprite constant:

    5acc/5b41/5bb6/5c2b:
        lea bx,[bx+4]                  ; bx = node+4, the POSITION descriptor
        mov al,0 ; lcall *0x61a
        mov ax,0xf88 / 0xf98 / 0xfa8 / 0xfb8 ; add ax,[0x7b9c]      ; ax = sprite id
        incw (bx) ; incw 2(bx)
        lcall *0x6c8                   ; <- AX = sprite id, BX = descriptor, both live
        decw (bx) ; decw 2(bx) ; ret

BX is provably live across the [0x61a] call: the asm bumps [bx] and [bx+2] immediately after it.

Two vectors are corrected, nine sites in all:

  * `[0x6c8]` -> FUN_0000_294d, FIVE parameters.  Four sites passed `(ax)`; now `(ax,0,0,bx,0)`, patch
    190's established form.
  * `[0x61a]` -> FUN_0000_11db(uint16_t bx, uint8_t al) -- a rect OUTLINE draw whose very first act is
    `FUN_0000_2d6d(bx)` and `(int16_t *)(dg + bx)`.  Five sites passed ONE argument (four passed `0`,
    584a passed the masked `ax & 0xff00`), so on native it drew from the rect at DGROUP:0 and on wasm
    the 1-argument signature did not match 11db's type and it drew nothing.  Now `(bx, 0)`.

NOT touched here, and left on board:0014: the sixth [0x61a] site, fist.c:65926 in FUN_1000_a547
(asm 1a584 `mov bx,0x967c; lcall *0x61a`).  BX is unambiguous there, but AL is NOT set before the call
-- the last write was `mov al,0x50` at 1a577, consumed by the [0x60a] call, with `call 0x15313` in
between.  AL is therefore ambient and must not be invented.

